{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/375840-character-idea-a-promethean-with-living-organ-donors","id":375840,"title":"Character Idea: A promethean with living organ donors","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-19T20:50:25-08:00","id":375840,"title":"Character Idea: A promethean with living organ donors","content":"So I was thinking, prometheans getting desperate enough to kill people for the creation rite is certainly mentioned, but it occurred to me: What if the would be demiurge isn't quite ruthless enough for murder, but just takes the parts they need from a living person?<br /> <br /> How would a promethean handle knowing that they were made not just of parts, but the parts of people who were left alive?<br /> <br /> People they might share memories with......<br /> <br /> Perhaps some different milestones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T21:35:19-08:00","id":375886,"title":"","content":"Works for things like lungs, kidneys, and the like, but what about hearts? Brains? Legs? Arms? Spines?<br /> <br /> It's a good idea, but it'd be a bitch to actually make work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T23:02:32-08:00","id":375910,"title":"","content":"There have been leg and arm transplants and limited spinal transplants. Brain transplants with monkeys, but this sounds more like a promethean running around lopping peoples limbs off and running away with them to their den. <br /> <br /> In This Symbiotic Fascination a character (a werewolf) takes things from people, representing him taking part of their soul, which ends up following him around. I'd probably make it into a more haunting story than most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T00:40:27-08:00","id":375952,"title":"","content":"-Did I ever tell you? My father didn't want to inconvenience his, ah... &quot;donors&quot; more than needed, so he took my right arm from a left-handed person and my left arm from a right-handed person. And that's why my handwriting is so bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T01:40:39-08:00","id":375977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/375840-character-idea-a-promethean-with-living-organ-donors?p=375910#post375910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There have been leg and arm transplants and limited spinal transplants. Brain transplants with monkeys, but this sounds more like a promethean running around lopping peoples limbs off and running away with them to their den.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say it wasn't medically possible to transplant limbs (although brains and such <i>would</i> kill the person, obviously), but I don't see many people willingly giving up their arm to a random guy so he can make himself a twisted perversion of a child/lover/brother.<br /> <br /> Unless it was diseased. Like, gengrene, or one of those infections that mean they have to amputate, or something? I mean, brains and such, still an issue, but that's a potentially interesting idea right there. Arm would still have traces of the infection, and overcoming that might be a milestone (more thematic than just taking some pills, obviously), but during that time they'd be walking around with that disease.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T04:46:07-08:00","id":376059,"title":"","content":"The urban legend about waking up in the bath with a kidney gone spring to mind.<br /> <br /> Will the Promethean's creator tell them that some or all of their parts come from the living, or is it something they'll piece together from getting what they thinks are flashes of corpse-memory but realising the truth as they see events that must be later than their creation?<br /> <br /> If the Promethean has the Spare Parts Bestowment, could it be possible to somehow return stolen parts to the original owners and replace them with parts from dead bodies? Even if it's not, could the victims (or the Promethean) <i>think</i> it is?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T23:48:52-08:00","id":378772,"title":"","content":"Thank you Nick, exactly the response I was hoping for, someone to see some story ideas from the idea.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T07:42:19-08:00","id":379025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/375840-character-idea-a-promethean-with-living-organ-donors?p=378772#post378772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Thank you Nick, exactly the response I was hoping for, someone to see some story ideas from the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you wanted <i>story ideas</i>? I thought you were asking if this were feasible/how it would work.<br /> <br /> Why limit yourself to being just one Promethean like that? What if it's a throng who create and maintain new members that way? And what if those who donated a part became immune to Disquiet from that Created?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T08:26:15-08:00","id":379050,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of a Promethean religious leader who uses his position to harvest the necessary components. Some people <i>will</i> have to die though, you can't simply harvest a brain and replace it you know.<br /> <br /> If the parts come from living beings, they'll be rebellious against their new master. They'll want to rip free of this body and go out to find their true master. It would be one weird Promethean for sure, but one terrifying Sublimati.<br /> <br /> Think about getting into a small town where people have been going missing since a few months, and suddently they all reapear, gone mad and limbs missing. That would freak people out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T01:42:22-08:00","id":387166,"title":"","content":"Umm.. Not 100% on this.. but what if it's an Unfleshed or Exotempore that is Doing this/having it done for... They are having a Body Built from living Parts that they can then use too interact with people.. Their &quot;Brain&quot; could still be whatever it normally is.. just Installed into the Head Cavity. This would make it even More Squick then usual for Prometheans...<br /> <br /> It also would negate the Need to harvest a Brain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T11:45:34-08:00","id":424338,"title":"","content":"What about using parts grown from stem cells for the vital organs? Would that create a proper Promethean or some kind of hybrid atrocity?<br /> <br /> Hell, what if you grew the entire body from stem cells (aka a clone)? What Lineage would it be, if it were a Promethean at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T14:10:04-08:00","id":424488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/375840-character-idea-a-promethean-with-living-organ-donors?p=387166#post387166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm.. Not 100% on this.. but what if it's an Unfleshed or Exotempore that is Doing this/having it done for... They are having a Body Built from living Parts that they can then use too interact with people.. Their &quot;Brain&quot; could still be whatever it normally is.. just Installed into the Head Cavity. This would make it even More Squick then usual for Prometheans...<br /> <br /> It also would negate the Need to harvest a Brain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couple this with an artificial heart, maybe slowly gather nerve and muscle tissue from the legs of paraplegics' legs (they weren't using it, anyway) for any muscles that can't be easily &quot;donated&quot;, bones from coral (which is actually used in some bone transplants due to how similar they are), maybe fit in an artificial liver machine into the body cavity, and you have a relatively &quot;green&quot; and &quot;low-cruelty&quot; Promethean!<br /> <br /> ...I think I have a new plot hook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T09:50:25-08:00","id":425358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/375840-character-idea-a-promethean-with-living-organ-donors?p=424488#post424488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couple this with an artificial heart, maybe slowly gather nerve and muscle tissue from the legs of paraplegics' legs (they weren't using it, anyway) for any muscles that can't be easily &quot;donated&quot;, bones from coral (which is actually used in some bone transplants due to how similar they are), maybe fit in an artificial liver machine into the body cavity, and you have a relatively &quot;green&quot; and &quot;low-cruelty&quot; Promethean!<br /> <br /> ...I think I have a new plot hook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prometheans by way of Chipotle Restaurants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T04:17:58-08:00","id":431241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/375840-character-idea-a-promethean-with-living-organ-donors?p=424338#post424338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about using parts grown from stem cells for the vital organs? Would that create a proper Promethean or some kind of hybrid atrocity?<br /> <br /> Hell, what if you grew the entire body from stem cells (aka a clone)? What Lineage would it be, if it were a Promethean at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it'd be a body... It be down to what the creator does to the body to give it it's Created existence that'll decide it's Lineage. Frankensteins tend to be the patchwork people, It wouldn't be a Zeka (they must be made from bodies killed by radiation poisoning), so depending on who the person was (a beauty could be a Galatea, a noble could be an Osiran, a hardy body can be a Tammuz, a spirit sighted could be an Ulgan) and the method of gifting them with new life will decide their Lineage. I'd go with Galatea though, just for the body being unmarred in any form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}